ng border tensions with South Korea and uncertainty over potential nuclear talks with the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: Department of Homeland Security data leak exposes details of more than 40,000 employees</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7e06bddc749e8647aaccdee3c3a90c312efeb37192451612f0ada4459206c0c</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T03:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-department-of-homeland-security-data-leak-exposes-details-of-more-than-40-000-employees/a-79791765--d74f0832e8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-department-of-homeland-security-data-leak-exposes-details-of-more-than-40-000-employees/a-79791765?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The leaked information reportedly includes names, phone numbers and email addresses of personnel across several US security agencies. This follows recent data breaches involving the FBI and the Defense Department.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU countries block Canada's 'associate membership' plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29713102ead034cd05f6e07885fb014c1a41728c56ced40a11d82a6f28784831</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T00:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-countries-block-canada-s-associate-membership-plan/a-79791601--4f2239f5da99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-countries-block-canada-s-associate-membership-plan/a-79791601?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen wanted to give Canada a special status within the EU. But Germany and other member states have raised objections ahead of a summit in Montreal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro lands in US, declares himself 'leader' of Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8802