n-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anders Fernstedt lives in London without any money. The Swedish native has built a most unusual home under the porch of a house worth over €200 million. How did that happen?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What Earth's sixth mass extinction event means for humans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eef0d1820970710bf67683097c77cc317407537577df48e3fabaf2159964242b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410--0a12d110aea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human activity is driving plants and animals to extinction at an unprecedented rate. As countries meet in Armenia to discuss ways to reverse nature loss, DW reveals how declining biodiversity is already harming people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>France: Young voters blase about Glucksmann's Socialists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bab67529d309c6b59c767a800b03b287bf5fb620af54014a9888ef0de0acc674</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159--5c98176d41f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-young-voters-blase-about-glucksmann-s-socialists/a-79684159?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Raphael Glucksmann wants to lead France's Socialists to power without working with the left-populist Jean-Luc Melenchon, who is particularly popular with young voters. How can the center-left candidate win them over?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's eight-hour workday under threat?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf40aaea351b6f554263c04a2486bcacdf263c8145bf0b947afdbfeca00c534b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T10:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984--28b0ad264d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-eight-hour-workday-under-threat/a-79680984?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Would you work 12 hours straight? The CDU/CSU and SPD are locked in a dispute over reforms to the Working Hours Act. Workplace flexibility, collective bargaining agreements and worker protection rules are at stake.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How reliant is Ukraine on the US-controlled Starlink internet service?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e15be590d2c01913e64f8dc8e8619d72dcff719a539cbae7fdb6aae7bb45f506</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729--6217d664b01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-reliant-is-ukraine-on-the-us-controlled-starlink-internet-service/a-79689729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kyiv keeps issuing warnings that the satellite internet system Starlink is being restricted in Ukraine. How dependent is the country on the system, and what would happen if it went down?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How big is Russia's threat against Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95dca309973523d68a409504af237ae734788ad3f508c5ee6d1acb38616f629b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426--e8db9669a70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts believe that, so far, Germany has been ill-prepared — both militarily and mentally — for Russian provocations. They also warn against the idea that ending support for Ukraine would make Germany safer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d963edd8250af21753546393471dbd385478827df4308249a56c423a7914600</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The Bundestag has debated the genocide Germany carried out in Namibia a century ago. But will it spur progress on addressing colonial crimes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4db8aceb51374e02205bcb47ff3bf2a8b080cf88a99a6cacfe010b8d9550f650</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur/a-79682388--50aa326f1793.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur-progress-on-addressing-colonial-crimes/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df5f8f960beff9ce8f7456041ece665ef693c998fb39e1ace2f792654a6b733c</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU promotes sovereign, trusted AI as it struggles to catch US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a51620b4832c30def5c036bb7fb4e8263b897e355927ca92d88b4ac1ef6b7267</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770--286aee32e70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At an international AI summit in Dublin, EU leaders promoted trusted and independent artificial intelligence. Critics question whether the bloc can close the gap with the US and China while maintaining strict regulation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543b318cf608ba0e336736e6a9c40514a7fadae37105f49311b4870b81162a90</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d71fe3f095c11fe8a44b187dd5964ec3a0afa78c6fe0349d8d9af2899a78086</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Labor Minister Bärbel Bas has stepped down, citing her need to grieve a loved one and leave behind the harsh realities of government. So how did German politics get so heated?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cda98b266b8cd1431773d05504362f84a2b1480d636ede22406ccea5ee835df3</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-d_rrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715--50ff40522ded.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-dörrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the world debates the dangers of artificial intelligence, filmmaker Doris Dörrie explores how humanoid robots could change the way we deal with aging, caregiving and how people choose to die.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of German gamblers could sue for their money back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e3e6704caa8046045c58bf069aaf01353c1779b7e83e66b5030a9be7efaad21</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844--bc7691d0e6e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German gamblers may finally be able to beat the house, thanks to new court rulings in the EU and in Germany. The decisions could help gambling addicts — but the legal road might be difficult.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Train station alcohol ban comes into force</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd966e269fd2b3e07220dd3f5b7bf9a82cc9ed70e17e496f2f32744c493e39cb</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807--e7db446fe401.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Consuming alcohol is no longer permitted at train stations in Germany, to improve the lot of travelers and staff alike. Coalition talks are restarting in Berlin, and an inmate is loose in Essen.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's elections matter for the planet. This is why</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a99106cb01fa77039c900a0ddebb712cf8d17c8cf8d3ea2289551256ede9c0f</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-elections-matter-for-the-planet-this-is-why/a-79659928--00329e582e5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-elections-matter-for-the-planet-this-is-why/a-79659928?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading back to the polls, but the impact could be felt worldwide. With the Amazon vital to the health of the planet, the election could help shape its future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Chinese tech brands are outpacing Western rivals from EVs to robot vacuums</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29e05303df9ff2ffa9eece5df0fa914cf5617ea31dec1cddf16fba068d8f6825</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-chinese-tech-brands-are-outpacing-western-rivals-from-evs-to-robot-vacuums/a-79646187--a8751d31a3ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-chinese-tech-brands-are-outpacing-western-rivals-from-evs-to-robot-vacuums/a-79646187?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From action cameras and smartphones to EVs and robot vacuums, Chinese brands are gaining ground worldwide, despite privacy and security concerns. What's driving their rise, and can European rivals keep up?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City, the UAE and the UK's OM in a political tangle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6892076a95d36151bdcdbd88d15e7dde52dcc59ec3e4d128d12b8954b1eddbc</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-om-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729--11ae1f17a0ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-om-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 20 years after arriving in England, Manchester City's UAE owners could exit amid cheating charges. That would pose a challenge for a city — and prime minister — closely tied to Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nord Stream trial opens in Germany, defense seeks dismissal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43efef5fa69a224506dde6372ecacdcb3afe6ef56cd50a80464faceec96b0d8c</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nord-stream-trial-opens-in-germany-defense-seeks-dismissal/a-79662942--840b7e9fd757.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nord-stream-trial-opens-in-germany-defense-seeks-dismissal/a-79662942?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serhii Kuznietsov is accused of attacking civilian infrastructure in the 2022 sabotage of the Russian gas pipeline to Germany. His lawyers called Nord Stream a military target, and said their client is sworn to secrecy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD forges a pro-Russia alliance with the BSW</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d537d8c85443920e119ff08d1d0d9f4e8bb078ebd3792a2e9a1842935aadd378</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-forges-a-pro-russia-alliance-with-the-bsw/a-79662413--9f342390b0ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-forges-a-pro-russia-alliance-with-the-bsw/a-79662413?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Saxony-Anhalt, the AfD and BSW are joining forces to push for negotiations with Moscow. What is driving this rapprochement?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's diesel deal with Russia is unlikely to significantly lower global fuel prices despite expectations of rapid relief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95eb0503e3dd0c09dee01b206ba8d84e55712ebdcd31aacc74c41069e990b733</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expect/a-79659601--8934faa2519e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expectations-of-rapid-relief/a-79659601?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the world's largest diesel exporter, the US benefits from high prices. At home, however, consumers are feeling the strain of rising living costs. Why Donald Trump's deal with Russia is unlikely to change that.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nord Stream: Germany puts suspected Ukrainian pipeline saboteur on trial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb54feaf4d29ea35c302904e270cc1526bc80a2bc552c30ae8804b3e0ccdb1ea</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nord-stream-germany-puts-suspected-ukrainian-pipeline-saboteur-on-trial/a-79647617--ad974b48960d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nord-stream-germany-puts-suspected-ukrainian-pipeline-saboteur-on-trial/a-79647617?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian citizen faces court in Hamburg, accused of attacking the Nord Stream gas pipelines in 2022. It raises questions about Kyiv's possible role in the explosions. German support for Ukraine is also under scrutiny.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Do non-German nationals commit more crimes than Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:372f5095d15b3264af23c19ef669faa9e579c9ced193cc6d7ababed6f887a606</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/do-non-german-nationals-commit-more-crimes-than-germans/a-79657273--07f237eb177a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/do-non-german-nationals-commit-more-crimes-than-germans/a-79657273?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">People without German passports appear more frequently in German police crime statistics than German nationals. A new study explains why.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>FIFPRO report highlights growing pains in women's football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bca6c044a1016699073dd0632ae21eaacaec02de7ea2c2233a7f7462e659768</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013--365fa34aee7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Expected global revenue of over $1 billion and new faces at the U17 World Cup show women's football is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden treasure in discarded wearable and fast tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:619febc60d9a7a1bdbc0c9207fe52a88115151921b89bd7976a4cf3cbebff4cf</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611--7010f2eed048.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sales of fast tech like mini fans and disposable e-vapes, as well as wearable health tech such as heart monitors and smartwatches are soaring. They're creating a new e-waste problem but are full of hidden treasure.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Formula 1: Rwanda to bring sport back to Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa6fbe6e64623b326e5cdf942b58a17c1e140ce2b807340091c9416252da107d</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217--ee284b399c6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last time Formula 1 hosted a race in Africa was way back in 1993. But a new track in Rwanda is set to host a Grand Prix in "the early 2030s," continuing the country’s investment in international sport.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c915a5261b9398990b6f01b837f2131ee85ff52fe1598951dbdd0dace144b8a</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fd94d916fc60b81f9aaac5b55ffc3fc73a20b40aca6cdf4bcb1a93b7e8950c2</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Labor Minister's resignation puts a spotlight on cracks within the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de775c991e1f7cf1f10e20ca97fc5e2bc6d9f0127dda76dae5573f1d003c735d</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823--1507ba6fa4a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-labor-minister-s-resignation-puts-a-spotlight-on-cracks-within-the-government/a-79645823?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the sudden resignation of Bärbel Bas as Labor Minister and co-chair of the Social Democratic Party, accusations are flying in Chancellor Merz's coalition government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pope lung nodule: Could it be cancer?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f49e5a900afcb12e8d6b9ebe846470f6800d0622c95a42781d5bbb57ad5aba9c</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503--9cf198017761.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The case of Pope Leo shows how small lung nodules are often found during routine health checks. Quick treatment is generally advised before nodules can grow to become larger life-threatening masses.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28923f0ebe181b5b98e2a8cabef1582cc6e51cd3bcf5cce19d0aa0dff14be2a8</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341--71931b21638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's win against Australia saw Ena Mahmutovic excel in goal. The 22-year-old Bayern Munich goalkeeper is considered the successor to Ann-Katrin Berger and is making a name for herself.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How green is Europe's urban public transport? A data-driven reality check</title><i