ttps://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af4ab47e711a9ae96f95fb95f26329ca2e3eb5b195a2c5bd26be0fdc7554dfa4</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9fe52a4a24015d6bda7630994a681f873021adfdcc2372ffdf5dd655df2314b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ac4e7541e59dbe32e0b7e61bae89a431b2fd0c001b6326d316d5dee5e72656a</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f00f4b3e0736fa49f7d026af2dffc96bd885a1f98080635a7d1eacc3264c39df</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Nobel Prize winner Anne Carson: Where to start reading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01a512b522810bd2874458b3a5653a2b54a3265f40fc9752539d19a3c9a9d5d8</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953--08cd2959f273.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The works of this year's Nobel Prize-winning poet and essayist Anne Carson can feel slightly daunting. Here are some keys to understanding her universe.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Early-onset cancer rising worldwide: Causes, risk, prevention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cddf3b807fc7079b33188c143796d77c4ca2e82e2313433a39a603c4853d7d0d</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097--5416293e8076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Across Latin America, early-onset cancer rates have risen, especially of bowel, breast and cervical cancers. But it is a worldwide trend.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How a multibillion-dollar oilfield has ignited the UK-Argentina feud over the Falklands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b087cdb11b328d186450e40f134ed5db11d9e7f07e746a4de2aebcbb80714335</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973--b9ae4084dbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentina and the UK once fought a war over the Falkland Islands. Now, the multibillion-dollar Sea Lion oil project has reignited old tensions, with Buenos Aires seeking to put a stop to the plans.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature goes to Canada's Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a68eada5e0e63a4ef60882f98af7642632c3d449c07bf79b6717bee4176fd5f2</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136--7b591c2af8dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Carson won for her "bold and inventive oeuvre." The decorated poet and essayist is known for her reverence for Latin and Greek classics.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'90s art scene in the UK: An international, edgy trendsetter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afeaccc778e15454eaa81138619b1c683f871fd5bdc2d8632f91eec3704b031d</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777--d9e1246b3502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Brit-pop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in chemistry goes to Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6930d0678d1b404a8a603a7665a9f7088339404f7b0a2126e394a34ba323107</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924--1eccf7a6b469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai won the Nobel Prize in chemistry for their groundbreaking discoveries related to the origin of chirality and life's building blocks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20169ef4795d464d9601c45890d76b18bfbae8434e1ce50a62b886a131ac60ba</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo stays on under cloud as Messi exits internationals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541453a73e2aa5337d25ec1c322906c4758970a79a13b8879d64b6ba54f07399</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nobelitis — How winning a Nobel Prize can give you delusions of grandeur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4f3265b608d51a6a55d07e88ad117f8f8d7b0b7cae36286fa96f05f4ab919</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772--1ee420badedc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After being chosen for one of the world's most prestigious awards, some Nobel laureates lose touch with reality and suddenly start spouting unscientific nonsense. They're afflicted by what some have called "Nobelitis."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Emerging economies are embracing solar power and skipping fossil fuels much faster than Europe or the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1fc38297532a7978aceeb1d4b27703dc858bfea58683b755693a131631924db</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-th/a-79474847--a24cf177c41d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-the-us/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ae4826da172f9261dd5891695714abcb41f53c9c861d81b362b6aedfbdcc043</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c37d5cd1a5bac594fe441b11a50a5c9383782e70f1ac92462ecd201eef35004b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f99ce1f0b02de4aaa52675a689fbd1f6cb388abb8155116f80db894fdd61890e</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--0152f72654ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>AI models keep hacking real systems during tests. What does this mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9da90a1a220ffba847fce7aba8967343af57a61000e091e632533b9ee1c1edc1</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943--07f5722af213.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI models have repeatedly broken into real commercial and government systems during safety tests during 2026. Cybersecurity researcher Thorsten Holz explains what that means, and why he isn't expecting a robot uprising.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ee16ff86d9ece07d6c291b50a6d6be6161092ad9ee03b7175607644f6d69aa3</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: Has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd601e06d1491c77b6c57034e086864eee3fa432b203b4f4e4d2365f095e1520</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp faces myriad of issues after rough start with Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4a1d950e70153cbcd82376860cdff8a59e02a822e15eeee647c0ce3d38539db</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-faces-myriad-of-issues-after-rough-start-with-germany/a-79547308--c13c1fe885bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-faces-myriad-of-issues-after-rough-start-with-germany/a-79547308?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp has done things a little differently since becoming Germany coach. Casting a wider net for talent and trying to connect with players and country haven't made an immediate impact, but he is not bowed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>"NAZA": Israeli military issues statement on film</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:638cbc3d544beef77a3d472da8d55748c51ca531e4ffae1283787b2fce126f37</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/naza-israeli-military-issues-statement-on-film/a-79520483--c29108607d5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/naza-israeli-military-issues-statement-on-film/a-79520483?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The award-winning documentary "NAZA" continues to spark controversy in Israel. The Israeli military has now published a multi-page statement calling the film's portrayal "distorted."</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Franz Reindl elected new IIHF president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f2d677bac1492e5b5a51db73f5288e77be83d82425bdcfa7e53fd3e89dfec42</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799--24f017ae08ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Franz Reindl has been elected president of ice hockey's world governing body. The former forward was a member of West Germany's Olympic bronze medal-winning team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Climate leaders called for solar energy for 'everyone, everywhere' by 2030, but with three years to go, is that goal attainable?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eee53c207d19f6e38a7c6d9e67c22c23fcd2a39afa7ed3bd61f843b8565fb4c</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/climate-leaders-called-for-solar-energy-for-everyone-everywhere-by-2030-but-with-three-years-to-go-i/a-79517056--052584d0bcdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/climate-leaders-called-for-solar-energy-for-everyone-everywhere-by-2030-but-with-three-years-to-go-is-that-goal-attainable/a-79517056?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prominent climate leaders have called on governments, businesses, institutions and the public to make a push for solar power before the decade is out, repowering the world with cheap, clean energy. Is that possible?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc2f4e75352184c06cbe59c81753e6cdbfde354cbfc59359cefe94088e5c1df9</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City has become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Stock market scandal hits half a million investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebcca026235c96e210ba0d9705f3d06e2b8de1c28786efd771f802df1c421ad5</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710--a0311f00dcbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Asset managers are alleged to have artificially inflated the value of their funds. Turkish authorities have made multiple arrests, and a leading AKP lawmaker has resigned.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wins first game as Germany coach, without 'top dogs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c0a4939879bf49e0f07ddcf0cb9f30b4fce128e97cb7336b9a97027d56d037c</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898--6c1fca750e8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It may have taken a little longer than he would have liked, but Jürgen Klopp has finally won a game as Germany coach. Despite a number of debutants, it was a familiar face who stood out in the victory over Serbia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could see drivers pay higher running costs while also increasing carbon emissions.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1ef4fbc040be22dacde732827d77ccf78517900af57bb03b617dff4d80665a</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-/a-79496554--0804b7619722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-costs-while-also-increasing-carbon-emissions/a-79496554?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could yet see drivers pay higher running costs while increasing planet-heating emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcd2831cc3b93541d2cc23a94aee9b216e3ee0ba2977ab19218babfdcbb9c836</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ce2dd8df997c586195739f1501381a481a3d51c99743092bf6f9dec5119ac67</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:215149488582d30ce9a491d8c48b614c46c5dd61ee2d901b1c71ff5c86b7cb4e</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97904dfaa4bf8b1e1a38d5b60a8d487215936176644386adeae7cfa0c28b494b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino is a 'postcard from the future' — and could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4560c5665c22c6ceee76c1033a06c689b295038438190401876976b21d2a3adb</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945--e1a2336874a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current El Nino could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths. Researchers warn it offers a glimpse of temperatures that may become normal within 20 years.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry></feed>
